# CPR and MCPR for GMT24

When the user types **`CPR`** or **`cpr`** (alone or as a clear request): commit current work if needed, push, redeploy production.

When the user types **`MCPR`** or **`mcpr`** (alone or as a clear request): **merge and CPR** — merge the current feature branch / open PR into `main`, then run the CPR redeploy path.

## Redeploy

The redeploy is **Git-triggered**: Vercel's GitHub integration builds every push to `main` as the production deployment (project `7-l-advisory/gmt24`, alias `gmt24.vercel.app`).

- Do **not** run `npx vercel --prod`. The `Vercel_token` secret cannot access the
  `7-l-advisory` team (SAML-enforced; token returns 404/403), so the CLI path fails.
- After pushing `main`, confirm the deploy instead:
  `gh api repos/classichot/GMT24/deployments --jq '.[0]'` → newest `Production` entry
  should carry the pushed SHA; its statuses endpoint reports `success` plus the
  deployment URL. Then spot-check `https://gmt24.vercel.app`.
- Report: commit hash, push status, deployment SHA/status, production URL.

## Merge (MCPR, or “merge and CPR”)

PR merges into `main` are done locally (`git worktree` + `--no-ff` merge + push);
the GitHub token cannot merge via API.

MCPR sequence:

1. If the working tree is dirty, commit on the feature branch (same safety checks as CPR / `pgit`; exclude secrets).
2. Push the feature branch.
3. Fetch `origin/main` and the feature branch.
4. Merge `--no-ff` into `main` via a worktree (`Merge pull request #N: <title>`).
5. Push `origin main` (this is the production redeploy).
6. Confirm the Vercel Production deployment and spot-check `https://gmt24.vercel.app`.
